# WIP: Kíli the Resourceful; intentionally not an applicable fix.
# Scryfall Oracle: "As long as you have an enduring story, you may pay {0}
# rather than pay the equip cost of the first equip ability you activate each
# turn."
#
# Baseline parsing recognizes Storied and the HasEnduringStory condition, but
# emits no cost modifier for this sentence; the Optional_YouMay swallow warning
# covers the line. Existing StaticMode::ReduceAbilityCost represents numeric
# reductions to activated costs, including once-per-turn reductions (Professor
# Hojo). StaticMode::CastWithAlternativeCost is spell-casting-only. Neither
# models an optional {0} replacement for an activated ability's equip cost.
#
# A correct general fix needs an alternative activation-cost choice in the
# shared activation-payment path, scoped to Equip abilities and gated by the
# player's enduring-story state, with a per-turn first-activation limit. Treating
# it as a large numeric reduction or as a spell alternative cost would be
# unsound. Relevant rules checked: CR 602.2b (activation follows casting-cost
# steps), CR 702.6a (Equip), and CR 702.195a (Storied).
#
# No parser or engine files were changed and no runtime test was run. Parked
# because this is shared activated-cost architecture for one card; the existing
# first-activation discount path is a useful analogue but does not supply an
# alternative activation-cost election.
